* Physical AI - Experiment 9: scaling network B 2->8->1
* Frozen random weights (seed 9). Weights were not edited.
* Matter Compiler v1 mapping: G=1e-05 quant=exact range=unconstrained
* Hidden: precision ReLU. Output: linear.
* Signed weights: G+/G- paths, I_diff = I+ - I- by KCL in SPICE.
* Bias: 1 V reference through G_SCALE*|b| onto the + or - path.
* G_SCALE = 1e-05
* shape: 2 -> 8 -> 1

Vin1 in1 0 DC 0
Vin2 in2 0 DC 0
Vref vref 0 DC 1

* --- neuron h1 ---
* h1 input 1 w=+0.292748916092307 w+  G = 2.92748916092307e-06 S  R = 341589.650731513 Ohm
Rh1p1 in1 h1p 341589.650731513
* h1 input 2 w=-0.041977234626618 w-  G = 4.1977234626618e-07 S  R = 2382243.63490084 Ohm
Rh1n2 in2 h1n 2382243.63490084
* h1 bias=-0.00679246096604694 b-  G = 6.79246096604694e-08 S  R = 14722204.5882728 Ohm
Rh1bn vref h1n 14722204.5882728
Vh1p h1p 0 DC 0
Vh1n h1n 0 DC 0
Fh1p 0 h1d Vh1p 1
Fh1n h1d 0 Vh1n 1
Vh1d h1d 0 DC 0
Hh1 h1lin 0 Vh1d 100000
Bh1 h1amp 0 V = max(-15, min(15, 100000 * v(h1lin, h1y)))
Dh1 h1amp h1y Dsi
RLh1 h1y 0 10000
Eh1 h1buf 0 h1y 0 1

